    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T17:01:13Z",
    "body": "Clarification from the reporter (via the user, 2026-11-19): the target is general **4-axis rotary 3D carving**, as on 4-axis CNC routers that carve a freeform model (for example a statue) out of a wood cylinder clamped on A. Reference video (a router maker's demo, not CAM software): https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OD2gwNOIQ_c\n\nSo the wanted operation is a rotary finish (and rough) for **any** model on a stated A axis, not only shapes of revolution:\n- the tool axis stays radial (perpendicular to A, through the axis);\n- passes run along X with A stepping between them, or as one continuous helix (X and A move together);\n- the tool height at each (X, A) comes from a drop along the radial direction onto the model (the radial version of a 3-axis parallel finish), with the existing radial gouge check against model, stock and fixture;\n- roughing removes the cylinder stock down to the model in radial steps.\n\nThis covers the helical rotor too (it is a special case). The stated-axis and rotary-heights parts stay as written here and in #2774. Spec from published 4-axis machining literature only; the video is the reporter's example of the result, not a source for the algorithm.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
